 qemu-server (9.2.7) trixie; urgency=medium
 
   * restore: bypass the host page cache when restoring to a ZFS zvol, both for
     Proxmox Backup Server and for VMA (vzdump) backups. Page writeback hands
     the restored data to the zvol one page at a time, which forces a
     read-modify-write of the surrounding volume block and can stall the I/O of
     other ZFS-backed guests for the duration of the restore.
 
   * d/control: depend on pve-qemu-kvm >= 11.0.3-3, which provides the
     pbs-restore option needed to skip the page cache on restore.
